(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
This research explores using physics to create computational music. In this \
project, we investigate the dynamics of a bouncing ball on a staircase and \
its application in generating musical notes using Mathematica. The objective \
of our research is to model the trajectory of a bouncing ball influenced by \
gravity and initial conditions, and to translate its kinetic behavior into \
musical expressions. Parameters such as the initial velocity of the ball, the \
number of stairs, and the number of balls are adjustable. As a result, the \
animation is capable of generating a variety of melodies.

The animation utilizes solutions to differential equations to simulate the \
ball\[CloseCurlyQuote]s motion, accounting for bounces and energy loss. The \
horizontal position of the ball (x-coordinate) determines the pitch of the \
generated musical notes, while the timing of the bounces dictates the rhythm. \
The result of our research is a three-dimensional animation of the bouncing \
ball displayed with a synchronized audio track playing.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellFrame->{{0, 0}, {0, 0.5}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.75],
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
